{"id":1190,"date":"2020-11-24T00:28:13","date_gmt":"2020-11-24T08:28:13","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1190"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:44","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:44","slug":"build-the-clapping-monkey-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-clapping-monkey-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Build the Clapping Monkey Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff124f\" name=\"6a22163ff124f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the body<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]For this entire step, make sure you&#8217;re paying attention to the orientation of the board and placement of all of the parts!<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Make a triangle out of two 4-hole metal frames and bolt a short standoff to the top angle. Bolt the bottom of the triangle to an upper corner of the blueboard. For the metal frame that&#8217;s actually on the corner, use a short standoff instead of a nut to secure the bolt.<\/li>\n<li>Repeat step 1 so you have 2 triangles on the blueboard. It should look a little like cat ears!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt two short L-frames right next to each other in the center of the blueboard. The edges that are sticking up should be facing the bottom of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a long L-frame to either side of the two short L-frames. The long L-frames should be positioned so there is one hole over the edge of the blueboard with the L-frames sticking out over the bottom.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt two short L-frames next to one of the long L-frames. They should be facing each other.<\/li>\n<li>Repeat step 5 with the other long L-frame.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1191&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff1363\" name=\"6a22163ff1363\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add the motor<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt the bottom motor casing to the short L-frames in the center of the blueboard.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a short L-frame to each short L-frame on the bottom of the blueboard. The new L-frames should be able to move easily, so don&#8217;t fasten the bolts too tightly!<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1193&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1194&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff13ca\" name=\"6a22163ff13ca\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add to the body<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Use long bolts and nylon nuts to attach two 7-hole metal frames to a horn bracket. Make sure the metal frames are angled correctly and do not cover the horn bracket&#8217;s center hole!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a short L-frame to the end of each 7-hole metal frame with nylon nuts. The ends of the short L-frames should be pointing down.<\/li>\n<li>Use a black screw to fasten the horn bracket to the motor. The metal frames and short L-frames should be pointing down.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1195&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1196&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff142e\" name=\"6a22163ff142e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build and add the arm<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt two short standoffs to the end of a 10-hole metal frame.<\/li>\n<li>Remember those short L-frames you attached allllll the way back in Step 2: Add the motor? Swing one up so it&#8217;s parallel to the short L-frame attached to the horn bracket.<\/li>\n<li>Fasten the 10-hole metal frame to the short L-frames using short standoffs to secure the bolts. The end with the two short standoffs should be sticking up in the air.<\/li>\n<li>Attach another 10-hole metal frame to the new short standoffs and secure them with two long standoffs.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1197&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1198&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1199&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff147b\" name=\"6a22163ff147b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build and add the other arm<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Good news: this step is just a mirror of the last step!<\/p>\n<p>Bad news: you might have to go back and look at the instructions again.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1200&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1201&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1202&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff14dc\" name=\"6a22163ff14dc\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add the hands and battery box<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt the center of a blueboard to each set of long standoffs.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the battery box to the two long L-frames on the bottom of the first blueboard.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1203&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1204&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff1534\" name=\"6a22163ff1534\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Build the head<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Bolt two short standoffs to the Smart Inventor board. Pay attention to placement!<\/li>\n<li>Bolt a blueboard to the short standoffs you just attached.<\/li>\n<li>Bolt the blueboard with the Smart Inventor board to the short L-frames close to the top of the first blueboard.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1205&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1206&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1207&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff1584\" name=\"6a22163ff1584\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add the eyes<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Remove the black rubber from the wheels.<\/li>\n<li>Remember the triangles you made back in Step 1: Build the body? Bolt the wheels to the short standoffs attached to those triangles.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1208&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff15db\" name=\"6a22163ff15db\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Wire the Clapping Monkey Bot<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You&#8217;re done! To wire your Clapping Monkey Bot properly, make sure the Smart Inventor Board is facing you:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The motor on your right is M1.<\/li>\n<li>The motor on your left is M2.<\/li>\n<li>Attach the motors to their respective spots on the Smart Inventor Board (M1, M2, M3, and M4 are all marked).<\/li>\n<li>Make sure that the red wires are the in the negative position (facing the inside) and that the black wires are in the positive position (facing the outside)!<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1209&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22163ff1640\" name=\"6a22163ff1640\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>Watch the video to see the Clapping Monkey Bot in action!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"activity2__spacer\">\n<div class=\"activity2__step-media\">\n<div class=\"activity2__step-media-preview\">\n<div class=\"activity2__step-media-constrain is-active\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=YE1wQ4ba44Y&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 Build the body [vc_column_text]For this entire step, make sure you're paying attention to the orientation of the board and placement of all of the parts! Make a&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/build-the-clapping-monkey-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1739,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1753,1777,1793,1617,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171],"lesson-tag":[2163,2168,2202,2172,2171],"class_list":["post-1190","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-build","lesson-tag-clapping-monkey-bot","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","module-monkey","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1190","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":3,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1190\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":6624,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1190\/revisions\/6624"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1739"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1190"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1190"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1190"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}